    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class (`AcceptanceBase` is abstract and `AuditLogCapture` is a helper).\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` with a per-city sequence.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`CustomerCode.java`** \u2014 the formatting utility now takes `city` as well and produces `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`. Extracted a private `prefix(...)` helper so the CITY3/LAST3 truncate-and-uppercase logic isn't duplicated.\n\n2. **`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 the sequence is now per-city (one more than the owners already in that city) instead of global. The count runs over `ownerRepository.findAll()` before the new owner is saved, so it reflects prior state.\n\n3. **`Cities.java`** (new) \u2014 a small helper mirroring the existing `Namesakes` helper, owning the \"same city\" matching (trimmed, whitespace-collapsed, case-insensitive). This keeps city-matching semantics out of `AssignCustomerCode`, matching the codebase's existing pattern (`CountNamesakes`/`Namesakes`).\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` descriptions and examples to the new format.\n\n**Values derived from `customerCode`:** `membershipNumber` in `OwnerMapper` builds on `owner.getCustomerCode()` directly (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`), so it automatically rebuilds on the new format \u2014 e.g. `LON-SMI-0007-M26`. No other value derives from `customerCode` (membership tier is based on namesakes/email, not the code).\n\nThe new format is at most 12 chars, well within the DB's `VARCHAR(20)` `customer_code` column.",
